,"detail":"回報率穩步領先同業基準"},{"id":4,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"應計利潤品質高 (CFO > 淨利潤)","passed":1,"detail":"真實現金流充沛，無虛報帳面獲利"},{"id":5,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"財務槓桿未惡化 (ΔLeverage ≤ 0)","passed":0,"detail":"總負債資產比率 = 75.3%"},{"id":6,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"短期流動性安全 (ΔLiquidity > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"流動比率 = 0.94"},{"id":7,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"股本未遭稀釋 (ΔShares ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"未大幅增發新股割韭菜"},{"id":8,"category":"營運效率","desc":"毛利率擴張 (ΔMargin > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":44.63,"default_fair_val":44.63,"premium_pct":623.1,"is_undervalued":false,"pe_trailing":24,"pe_forward":21.1,"pb_trailing":53,"pb_forward":47.7,"div_yield":0,"ps_ratio":23.8,"fcf_to_ev":1.05,"fcf_to_mcap":1.05,"liab_to_assets":75.3,"cash_to_assets":27,"current_ratio":0.94,"roe":18,"roa":8,"moat":{"ticker":"SNOW","period":"2027Q2","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Snowflake 的品牌定價權主要體現在其雲端數據倉儲平台的領先地位和技術創新上。客戶因其平台的彈性、可擴展性和易用性而願意支付溢價。然而，與傳統軟體巨頭相比，其品牌忠誠度仍在建立中，且面臨來自雲端服務商（AWS, Azure, GCP）的整合競爭，這限制了其定價權的絕對強度。","comment_en":"Snowflake's brand pricing power stems from its leading position and technological innovation in cloud data warehousing. Customers are willing to pay a premium for its platform's flexibility, scalability, and ease of use. However, compared to established software giants, its brand loyalty is still developing, and it faces integration competition from cloud providers (AWS, Azure, GCP), which limits the absolute strength of its pricing power."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":5,"comment_zh":"Snowflake 的核心競爭力在於其創新的雲端原生架構和數據共享技術，而非傳統意義上的專利壁壘。雖然其技術具有獨特性，但軟體領域的專利保護相對較弱，且容易被模仿或被更先進的技術取代。監管風險相對較低，但其技術迭代速度要求公司持續投入研發以維持領先。","comment_en":"Snowflake's core competitive advantage lies in its innovative cloud-native architecture and data sharing technology, rather than traditional patents. While its technology is unique, patent protection in the software sector is relatively weak and easily imitated or superseded by more advanced technologies. Regulatory risks are relatively low, but its rapid technological iteration requires continuous R&D investment to maintain leadership."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"Snowflake 構建了顯著的轉換成本壁壘。一旦企業將其數據基礎設施遷移至 Snowflake，並將關鍵業務流程與之整合，後續的遷移成本將極高，涉及數據遷移、應用程式重寫、員工再培訓等多方面。這種深度整合和對平台依賴性，為 Snowflake 提供了強大的客戶黏性。","comment_en":"Snowflake has built significant switching cost barriers. Once enterprises migrate their data infrastructure to Snowflake and integrate critical business processes, the subsequent migration costs become extremely high, involving data migration, application rewriting, and employee retraining. This deep integration and platform dependency provide Snowflake with strong customer stickiness."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Snowflake 的數據共享功能創造了網絡效應。隨著更多數據提供者和數據消費者加入其平台，數據的價值和可用性呈指數級增長，吸引更多用戶，形成正向循環。這種數據交換的生態系統增強了平台的吸引力，並對新進入者構成挑戰。","comment_en":"Snowflake's data sharing capabilities create network effects. As more data providers and consumers join its platform, the value and availability of data grow exponentially, attracting more users and forming a virtuous cycle. This data exchange ecosystem enhances the platform's attractiveness and poses a challenge to new entrants."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Snowflake 的規模經濟體現在其雲端基礎設施的優化和運營效率上。透過集中化的資源管理和彈性的計算能力，它能為客戶提供比自建數據中心更具成本效益的解決方案。然而，其成本結構仍受雲端基礎設施提供商的定價影響，且與大型雲端服務商相比，規模優勢並非絕對領先。","comment_en":"Snowflake's economies of scale are reflected in the optimization of its cloud infrastructure and operational efficiency. Through centralized resource management and elastic computing power, it can offer customers more cost-effective solutions than on-premises data centers. However, its cost structure is still influenced by cloud infrastructure provider pricing, and its scale advantage is not absolutely leading compared to major cloud service providers."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"Snowflake 的業務模式高度依賴於雲端基礎設施，其核心資產是軟體技術和數據平台，而非特定地理位置的實體資產。因此，在這一維度上，其護城河非常薄弱，沒有顯著的地理優勢或獨特的實體資產構成壁壘。","comment_en":"Snowflake's business model relies heavily on cloud infrastructure; its core assets are software technology and its data platform, not physical assets in specific geographic locations. Therefore, its moat in this dimension is very weak, with no significant geographical advantages or unique physical assets forming barriers."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"Snowflake 在雲端數據倉儲領域展現了卓越的運營效率。其平台設計旨在提供彈性、高性能和低延遲的數據處理能力，同時通過按需付費模式優化客戶成本。持續的技術投入和優化使其能夠高效地服務大量客戶，並快速響應市場需求。","comment_en":"Snowflake demonstrates excellent operational efficiency in the cloud data warehousing space. Its platform is designed for elastic, high-performance, and low-latency data processing, while optimizing customer costs through a pay-as-you-go model. Continuous technological investment and optimization enable it to serve a large customer base efficiently and respond quickly to market demands."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Snowflake 的資本配置策略著重於研發投入以維持技術領先，並積極拓展市場份額。雖然其現金流強勁，但相較於成熟的價值型公司，其資本配置更側重於成長和創新，而非大規模的股息或股票回購。管理層在平衡增長與盈利能力方面表現出一定的謹慎。","comment_en":"Snowflake's capital allocation strategy focuses on R&D investment to maintain technological leadership and aggressively expand market share. While its cash flow is strong, compared to mature value companies, its capital allocation prioritizes growth and innovation over substantial dividends or share buybacks. Management shows a degree of prudence in balancing growth with profitability."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"Snowflake 透過其強大的平台功能、持續的創新以及顯著的轉換成本，實現了非常高的客戶留存率。一旦客戶深度整合其數據工作流程，並依賴 Snowflake 的數據共享和分析能力，轉換到競爭對手的可能性就大大降低。客戶對其平台的依賴性是其留存的關鍵。","comment_en":"Snowflake achieves very high customer retention rates through its robust platform features, continuous innovation, and significant switching costs. Once customers deeply integrate their data workflows and rely on Snowflake's data sharing and analytics capabilities, the likelihood of switching to competitors is greatly reduced. Customer dependency on its platform is key to its retention."},"m10_durability":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Snowflake 的長期可持續性取決於其持續創新的能力和應對雲端市場變化的敏捷性。雖然其技術架構具有前瞻性，但軟體行業的快速變化意味著其領先地位可能受到挑戰。其商業模式的韌性在於其對數據驅動經濟的關鍵作用，但需要警惕來自大型雲端供應商的潛在整合威脅。","comment_en":"Snowflake's long-term sustainability depends on its ability to innovate continuously and adapt agilely to changes in the cloud market. While its technological architecture is forward-looking, the rapid evolution of the software industry means its leading position could be challenged. The resilience of its business model lies in its critical role in the data-driven economy, but potential integration threats from major cloud providers must be monitored."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"Snowflake 的護城河主要建立在其技術創新、顯著的轉換成本以及數據共享所帶來的網絡效應之上，使其在雲端數據倉儲領域具有強大的競爭優勢。這是一種基於技術和生態系統的「收費橋」模式，客戶因深度整合和數據價值而難以離開。然而，其品牌定價權和規模成本優勢相較於傳統巨頭仍有提升空間，且缺乏傳統的專利或地理資產壁壘。其長期可持續性依賴於持續的技術迭代和對抗雲端巨頭整合的能力。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"Snowflake's moat is primarily built on technological innovation, significant switching costs, and network effects derived from data sharing, granting it a strong competitive advantage in cloud data warehousing. This resembles a 'toll bridge' model based on technology and ecosystem, where customers find it difficult to leave due to deep integration and data value. However, its brand pricing power and scale cost advantages have room for improvement compared to traditional giants, and it lacks traditional patent or geographical asset barriers. Its long-term sustainability hinges on continuous technological iteration and the ability to counter integration by cloud behemoths.","evidenceHash":"f785a4cc46befb581b5feeee911ead5beac6e9c59e844106657cf2f1c035e010","assessmentPolicy":"us-buffett-moat-v3"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null},"fScore":{"score":6,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2026-01-31","period":"FY 2026","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"superRobust","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-28T14:40:26.418Z","evidenceHash":"60de9e1aa2d303f5feef98b162a9a4c913bf8232d1d7ff893011bda9ffe4fb62"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2026-01-31","period":"FY 2026","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-28T14:40:26.418Z","evidenceHash":"60de9e1aa2d303f5feef98b162a9a4c913bf8232d1d7ff893011bda9ffe4fb62"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/SNOW.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/SNOW.png","website":"https://www.snowflake.com","ceo":"Sridhar Ramaswamy","full_time_employees":"9394","description":"Snowflake Inc. delivers a cloud-centric data platform to customers across both the United States and international markets. The company's core offering, known as the Data Cloud, enables users to unify disparate data sources into a singular, reliable foundation. This unified data then facilitates the extraction of crucial business intelligence, the creation of innovative data-driven applications, and secure data sharing. This adaptable platform serves a wide array of organizations, encompassing various sizes and industries. Originating in 2012, the enterprise was initially recognized as Snowflake Computing, Inc., before officially rebranding to Snowflake Inc. in April 2019. Its principal operations are conducted from Bozeman, Montana.","description_en":"Snowflake Inc. delivers a cloud-centric data platform to customers across both the United States and international markets. The company's core offering, known as the Data Cloud, enables users to unify disparate data sources into a singular, reliable foundation. This unified data then facilitates the extraction of crucial business intelligence, the creation of innovative data-driven applications, and secure data sharing. This adaptable platform serves a wide array of organizations, encompassing various sizes and industries. Originating in 2012, the enterprise was initially recognized as Snowflake Computing, Inc., before officially rebranding to Snowflake Inc. in April 2019. Its principal operations are conducted from Bozeman, Montana.","description_zh":"**Snowflake Inc. (SNOW) 業務營運概述**\n\nSnowflake Inc. 提供以雲端為核心的數據平台，服務橫跨美國及國際市場。其核心產品「Data Cloud」旨在協助客戶整合分散的數據來源，建立單一、可靠的數據基礎。此統一數據基礎進而支援企業提取關鍵商業洞察、開發創新數據驅動應用程式，並實現安全的數據共享。\n\n該平台具備高度彈性，可滿足不同規模及產業的多元化組織需求。Snowflake 的營運模式著重於提供一個可擴展、高效能且易於使用的雲端數據解決方案，讓客戶無需自行管理複雜的基礎設施。透過其獨特的雲端架構，Snowflake 實現了計算與儲存的分離，提供卓越的效能與成本效益，成為現代數據管理與分析的關鍵平台。","address":"135 Constitution Drive","city":"Menlo Park","state":"CA","zip":"94025","country":"US","phone":"844 766 9355","full_address":"135 Constitution Drive, Menlo Park, CA 94025, US","range_52w":"118.3-384.56","year_high":384.56,"year_low":118.3,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":118.3,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-10-21","name":"Slootman Frank","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":300000,"price":8.88,"total_val":2.66},{"date":"2026-10-21","name":"Slootman Frank","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":300000,"price":8.88,"total_val":2.66},{"date":"2026-10-21","name":"Slootman Frank","title":"director","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":9220,"price":311.06,"total_val":2.87},{"date":"2026-10-21","name":"Slootman Frank","title":"director","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":11959,"price":312.4,"total_val":3.74},{"date":"2026-10-21","name":"Slootman Frank","title":"director","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":4250,"price":312.86,"total_val":1.33},{"date":"2026-10-21","name":"Slootman Frank","title":"director","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":22761,"price":314.46,"total_val":7.16},{"date":"2026-10-21","name":"Slootman Frank","title":"director","is_buy":false,"action":